.TH earth 1X MOTIF "Demonstration programs"
.SH NAME
\*Learth\*O\ - a resizable globe animation demo.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.sS
\*Learth\*O [-speed tenths-rpm] [-fps number]
.sE
.SH DESCRIPTION
\*LEarth\*O
displays a rotating globe in a decorated, movable, resizable window with a
black background. Modern light/dark profiles project one high-resolution
world map onto a shaded sphere. Classic profiles use the original artwork.
Right-click the globe to toggle an inline, normally themed speed slider below
it. Left-click without dragging to stop. Drag left/right and release to set
spin direction and speed; holding still before release stops. Automatic
rotation is suspended throughout pointer control. The mouse wheel zooms in or
out in 2-percent steps around the center of the globe area (5 to 200 percent).

The speed argument is an integer in tenths of revolutions per minute, from
-200 to 200. The default is 5 (0.5 RPM, one turn every two minutes). Zero
pauses; negative values reverse rotation. The slider displays decimal RPM.
The -fps argument independently sets presentation cadence from 1 to 120 FPS
(default 30). Out-of-range values are clamped. A monotonic clock determines
rotation, so dropped frames do not alter angular speed or create catch-up
bursts. Pausing removes the animation timer.

.SH X Defaults
The class of this application is \fIXmdEarth\fR.  

Earth supports the following application resources:
      speed, fps, background, foreground.
